### Enrollment Service requests for IntelliJ's built-in HTTP Client.
### Needs the student-service (seed data) and course-service running.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8083

### 1. Enroll student 1 in course 1 (expect 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 1, "courseId": 1 }

### 1b. Same request again (expect 409 duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 1, "courseId": 1 }

### 1c. Missing fields (expect 400 with field errors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 1d. Inactive student 5 (expect 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 5, "courseId": 1 }

### 1e. Unknown student (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 99, "courseId": 1 }

### 1f. Unknown course (expect 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 1, "courseId": 99 }

### 1g. Full course CS499 (expect 409 "is full")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 1, "courseId": 7 }

### 1h. DRAFT course PH310 (expect 409 "not open")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 1, "courseId": 8 }

### 2. Is student 1 enrolled in course 1?
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/check?studentId=1&courseId=1

### 2b. Missing parameter (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/check?studentId=1

### 3a. List everything
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments

### 3b. Roster of course 1 (student ids)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments?courseId=1&status=ENROLLED

### 3c. One student's enrollments, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments?studentId=1&sortBy=enrolledAt&direction=desc

### 3d. Invalid status (expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments?status=BOGUS

### 4. Student 1's courses with course details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/student/1/courses

### 5. Get one enrollment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/1

### 5b. Not found (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/999

### 6. Drop enrollment 1 (expect 200, seat released)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/1/drop

### 6b. Drop again (expect 409, no second seat released)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/1/drop

### 6c. Re-enroll after drop (expect 201, same enrollment id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "studentId": 1, "courseId": 1 }

### 7. Complete an enrollment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/enrollments/1/complete

### 8. Course side: verify the seat counter after the steps above
GET http://localhost:8082/api/courses/1

### 9. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health
